	(text "UWB Array -- 4x DW3210 (A0 center + A1-A3 outer)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 115.062 1.27 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
		)
		(uuid "66666666-0000-4000-8000-000000000001")
	)
	(text "Placement only: no wires or global labels yet, same convention as this\nboard's other unwired sheets.\n\nTHE FOUR ANCHORS ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE PEERS.\n  U4 = A0, the CENTER anchor. Does two-way ranging with the wristband and\n       produces the RANGE to the tag.\n  U5-U7 = A1-A3, the OUTER anchors. They timestamp the SAME wristband\n       transmission and produce TDoA against A0, which gives DIRECTION.\nOne tag transmission, four measurements. See docs/positioning.md.\n\nWhy discrete DW3210 and not the DWM3000 module this sheet used to hold:\nTDoA compares timestamps across receivers, so they must share a time base\n-- 1ns of clock error is 30cm of position error. The module exposes no\nclock pin and its crystal is unreachable, so four of them cannot be\nsynchronised at any price. The bare IC can: XTI (pin 21) is documented as\nan external-reference overdrive input. All four XTI pins are driven from\nthe one TCXO on clock_dist.kicad_sch.\n\nDW3210 is the QFN40 5x5mm NON-PDoA variant. Deliberately NOT DW3110, which\nis the 52-ball WLCSP the module is built on and is not hand-assemblable."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 117.856 26.416 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "66666666-0000-4000-8000-000000000002")
	)
	(text "PER-ANCHOR CONNECTIONS, still to be wired:\n  RF1 (pin 18)  -> 2pF series cap -> SMA connector -> ~1-2m coax -> antenna.\n                   CH5 is 6489.6MHz, ABOVE U.FL's 6GHz rating: SMA only.\n  RF2 (pin 13)  -> unused on the non-PDoA variant. No cap, but terminate\n                   into 50 ohm through a 50 ohm trace.\n  XTI (pin 21)  -> 2200pF AC coupling from the clock buffer (clock_dist).\n  XTO (pin 22)  -> 1pF to ground. Required ONLY because an external clock\n                   is used (clock_dist holds C28-C31 for this).\n  SPI           -> SPICLK 34, SPIMOSI 35, SPIMISO 36 shared across all four;\n                   SPICSn 37 individually to the host.\n  IRQ (pin 1)   -> individually to the host.\n  RSTn (pin 33) -> shared reset from the host.\n\nSUPPLIES (all from +3V3_SYS, regulation.kicad_sch):\n  VDD1 pin 29 (1.62-3.6V) is the main supply and also feeds WAKEUP, EXTON,\n  RSTn and the SPI I/O. VDD2a pin 28 and VDD2b pin 23 are 2.4-3.6V; the\n  datasheet notes the WLCSP equivalents need ferrite isolation from each\n  other, so check that applies on QFN before merging them. VDD3 pin 26 is\n  1.5-3.6V.\n  VTX_D pin 27 and VIO_D pin 38 are NOT supply inputs -- they are decoupling\n  pins, each needing its own capacitor to ground. Do not tie them to a rail.\n\nDECOUPLING IS NOT YET PLACED. The old C8-C19 were sized for a module with\none VDD3V3 rail and do not map onto this IC's separate VDD1/VDD2/VDD3 rails\nplus two decoupling pins. Re-derive from the DW3000 datasheet before wiring."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 116.586 75.184 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "66666666-0000-4000-8000-000000000003")
	)
	(text "LAYOUT (Section 7.3, not actionable until layout starts): RF1/RF2 must be\n50 ohm impedance-controlled; ground removed from under the chip on the top\nlayer and inner layer 1; first solid ground copper at least 0.25mm below the\ntop layer. This forces a controlled-impedance stackup of at least 4 layers."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 114.046 107.696 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "66666666-0000-4000-8000-000000000004")
	)
